WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Thank you.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:59.980
Thank you.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:29.980
Thank you.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Thank you.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:47.939
Hello, Clark.

00:01:49.039 --> 00:01:50.480
My name is Kara.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.219
I'm from Krypton.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.819
Thank you.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:15.439
Thank you.

00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:15.840
Thank you.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:29.759
Thank you.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:39.819
I made this whole world shine for you

00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:45.620
Yeah, yeah, come on

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:52.219
Kara, I don't know where you heard about Krypton,

00:02:52.979 --> 00:02:55.420
but an astronomer told me that planet was destroyed.

00:02:55.979 --> 00:02:59.680
Its physical form is gone, but it still lives on through us.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.319
Here, this will warm you up.

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:09.240
It's hot tea.

00:03:13.039 --> 00:03:17.000
Young lady, I'm sure that your parents are very worried about you.

00:03:17.039 --> 00:03:17.939
Why don't you let us call them?

00:03:18.199 --> 00:03:19.000
There's no one to call.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.099
Well, you can't sleep out in the field.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:22.599
You'll stay with us tonight.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.219
Thank you.

00:03:25.039 --> 00:03:26.439
I heard you were very kind.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.020
How exactly did you get here?

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:29.979
I came here to see you.

00:03:29.979 --> 00:03:31.560
I came through a passage in the cave wall.

00:03:33.139 --> 00:03:34.379
A passage from where?

00:03:36.019 --> 00:03:38.479
A place where all your questions will be answered.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.060
Where you don't have to hide your true self.

00:03:42.299 --> 00:03:45.219
Look, if you really are from some distant planet,

00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:46.359
why don't you do us a favor, huh?

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:49.439
Give us a display of all of your special abilities.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:51.560
Dad.

00:03:51.799 --> 00:03:52.079
Clark.

00:03:53.219 --> 00:03:56.299
You told me yourself that Pete's being harassed by the FBI.

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:59.039
How do we know that this isn't just some sort of a ploy?

00:03:59.979 --> 00:04:01.239
Jonathan Kent.

00:04:01.539 --> 00:04:03.539
You have no place in this conversation.

00:04:04.679 --> 00:04:07.679
I will show Kal-El all he needs to see in due time.

00:04:08.899 --> 00:04:10.139
Where did you hear that name?

00:04:13.939 --> 00:04:15.539
It was given to you at birth.

00:04:16.899 --> 00:04:17.759
Why are you here?

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.300
To take you home.

00:04:26.719 --> 00:04:27.159
Clark?

00:04:27.159 --> 00:04:27.259
Clark?

00:04:29.019 --> 00:04:29.379
Lex.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.700
Hey, do you have a second?

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:33.540
This is, um...

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:42.280
Good time, isn't he?

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.259
I thought you'd be out celebrating.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.960
Your dad's finally behind bars.

00:04:59.959 --> 00:05:04.120
My father has a battalion of lawyers more powerful than Caesar's army.

00:05:04.299 --> 00:05:05.939
He'll be out on bail unless for 48 hours.

00:05:06.599 --> 00:05:09.839
I don't think the judge is gonna let a murderer back out on the street.

00:05:10.159 --> 00:05:11.839
Clark, the only way he'll be denied bail

00:05:11.839 --> 00:05:14.899
is if there's evidence at his bail hearing that he's an imminent threat to society.

00:05:15.019 --> 00:05:16.240
What about Chloe's voicemail?

00:05:16.939 --> 00:05:18.599
The one with your dad's confession on it?

00:05:18.599 --> 00:05:19.539
That can be pretty damaging.

00:05:20.179 --> 00:05:22.039
It will be, for the grand jury.

00:05:22.959 --> 00:05:25.359
But in order to deny him bail, they need eyewitnesses.

00:05:25.919 --> 00:05:28.279
People have seen my father actually inflict harm.

00:05:29.079 --> 00:05:29.439
Unfortunately, anyone who's been in the same situation as me has.

00:05:29.439 --> 00:05:29.519
Unfortunately, anyone who's been in the same situation as me has.

00:05:29.519 --> 00:05:31.379
Unfortunately, anyone who's been privy to his darkest moments

00:05:31.379 --> 00:05:33.259
is either dead or unwilling to come forward.

00:05:36.419 --> 00:05:37.279
I'll come forward.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.500
I appreciate the support, Clark, but they need an eyewitness.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.560
I saw him at Belle Reve.

00:05:46.859 --> 00:05:49.899
I saw him order the doctor to increase your electroshock voltage.

00:05:52.519 --> 00:05:54.740
Even when the doctor said it could turn you into a vegetable.

00:05:58.459 --> 00:05:59.500
How could you have seen that?

00:05:59.519 --> 00:06:05.839
I snuck in to try to save you, but I was too late.

00:06:08.539 --> 00:06:11.839
You knew all along my father murdered his parents, didn't you?

00:06:13.379 --> 00:06:15.159
And you never told me, Lex.

00:06:15.299 --> 00:06:18.039
I always assumed there was a tacit agreement among friends

00:06:18.039 --> 00:06:20.060
to share that kind of information with each other.

00:06:20.159 --> 00:06:21.519
Not when it can get your friend killed.

00:06:23.939 --> 00:06:27.219
Lex, your father threw you in a mental institution and fried your brain.

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:27.259
I don't know.

00:06:27.259 --> 00:06:27.300
I don't know what happened.

00:06:28.819 --> 00:06:31.039
If you found that out all over again, I thought he might kill you,

00:06:31.079 --> 00:06:32.039
and I couldn't live with that.

00:06:42.279 --> 00:06:43.420
You're a good friend, Clark.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.339
If you tell the judge what you just told me,

00:06:48.159 --> 00:06:52.319
my father will be exchanging his Armani for an orange jumpsuit.

00:06:55.099 --> 00:06:56.459
I'll be there. You can count on it.

00:06:57.259 --> 00:06:59.800
It was my fault.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:01.959
Six-one, clear.

00:07:02.019 --> 00:07:02.599
Coming up.

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:08.639
I thought we had a deal, loader.

00:07:08.719 --> 00:07:10.360
Look, I tipped you off on your son's wire.

00:07:10.779 --> 00:07:13.420
I made sure any discriminating recordings disappeared into the ether.

00:07:13.819 --> 00:07:16.180
I can't control some bleached blonde, Polish or wannabe

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.439
from dredging up evidence for a decades-old homicide.

00:07:19.459 --> 00:07:22.620
And our other investigation, Lex's friend, what's the status of that?

00:07:24.199 --> 00:07:25.300
You're a piece of work.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:26.879
In case you haven't noticed,

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:29.019
you're a hop, skip, and a jump away from death row.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.800
And no hick farm kid's secret's gonna be able to save your ass.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:34.620
This is just an inconvenience.

00:07:34.699 --> 00:07:36.420
I'll be out on bail in a couple of hours.

00:07:36.759 --> 00:07:38.459
And I expect you to send me the information

00:07:38.459 --> 00:07:40.120
you've gathered so far on Clark Kent.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.980
You can expect to be waiting for a very long time.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.699
Our deal's over, Mr. Luther.

00:07:48.219 --> 00:07:50.519
You're venturing into dangerous waters, Loader.

00:07:51.279 --> 00:07:52.600
I'm a pretty decent swimmer.

00:07:53.699 --> 00:07:54.180
Night-night.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:57.360
Opening six-one.

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:07.560
You shouldn't involve yourself in their problems.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.920
Lex is my friend. I want to help him.

00:08:11.939 --> 00:08:12.960
You can't trust him.

00:08:13.899 --> 00:08:14.920
You don't know him.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:16.740
I don't have to.

00:08:17.699 --> 00:08:19.920
It's human nature. It's just who they are.

00:08:20.519 --> 00:08:22.519
They happen to be the people that I care about.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.160
Which is why it'll be that much harder for you

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.680
when they all betray you.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.540
I can understand why you're scared.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.100
This is all you know.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:36.560
But you're not meant for this world, Callow.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:38.860
You were meant for mine.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.259
My name's Clark.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.740
And why should I believe anything you say?

00:08:44.899 --> 00:08:46.100
Because it's the truth.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:47.139
Really?

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.600
Why don't you start by telling me

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:51.360
where you've been for the last 14 years?

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.080
If you join me,

00:08:54.159 --> 00:08:57.159
all your questions will be answered.

00:08:59.539 --> 00:09:00.919
That's not good enough.

00:09:03.379 --> 00:09:04.159
Callow, wait.

00:09:06.159 --> 00:09:07.339
Come with me.

00:09:24.159 --> 00:09:26.639
Why do you do this?

00:09:26.639 --> 00:09:27.299
Tell me.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:28.240
I can't help it.

00:09:28.539 --> 00:09:29.039
Your will.

00:09:29.079 --> 00:09:30.939
This is why you can't fly.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.779
This is why you get to die.

00:09:34.419 --> 00:09:34.919
Come!

00:09:34.919 --> 00:09:35.679
juegos

00:09:35.679 --> 00:09:36.379
?

00:09:36.379 --> 00:09:37.299
Questo è comello

00:09:38.299 --> 00:09:41.379
comello

00:09:41.679 --> 00:09:44.539
comello

00:09:44.539 --> 00:09:45.839
How are you doing this?

00:09:46.639 --> 00:09:47.719
You're doing it too.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.039
I can't fly.

00:09:51.039 --> 00:09:53.879
Miss Fissure wasn't here last week.

00:09:54.599 --> 00:09:56.120
It opened to release me.

00:09:57.179 --> 00:09:58.599
It'll open again when we go.

00:10:00.719 --> 00:10:02.459
What makes you think I don't like this world?

00:10:03.919 --> 00:10:06.319
I can sense how sad you are, Kal-El.

00:10:07.439 --> 00:10:09.620
Not a day goes by where you don't feel like an outsider.

00:10:10.879 --> 00:10:14.759
Even those closest to you will never truly understand you.

00:10:18.959 --> 00:10:20.679
But it doesn't have to be that way.

00:10:21.039 --> 00:10:22.039
It's not.

00:10:27.679 --> 00:10:29.339
You've been down here ever since the meteor shower?

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:30.419
Yes.

00:10:31.259 --> 00:10:33.379
Waiting for the time when he knew you'd be ready.

00:10:34.159 --> 00:10:34.459
He?

00:10:35.139 --> 00:10:36.139
Your birth father.

00:10:37.279 --> 00:10:37.679
Jor-El.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.139
He died in Krypton.

00:10:40.899 --> 00:10:42.039
Yes, but...

00:10:42.799 --> 00:10:45.279
his spirit and will live on inside these walls.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:49.500
You should have known.

00:10:51.039 --> 00:10:53.039
He's not the monster that you imagine.

00:10:53.039 --> 00:10:55.039
He saved your life.

00:10:55.039 --> 00:10:57.039
To turn me into something I never wanted to be.

00:10:57.039 --> 00:10:59.039
You may think you know your destiny,

00:10:59.039 --> 00:11:01.039
but you have no idea what greatness lies ahead of you.

00:11:01.039 --> 00:11:03.039
Then why don't you tell me?

00:11:03.039 --> 00:11:05.039
I'm only here to help your transition.

00:11:05.039 --> 00:11:07.039
Everything that you want to know lies through there.

00:11:07.039 --> 00:11:09.039
I'm here to help you.

00:11:09.039 --> 00:11:11.039
I'm here to help you.

00:11:11.039 --> 00:11:13.039
I'm here to help you.

00:11:13.039 --> 00:11:15.039
I'm here to help you.

00:11:15.039 --> 00:11:17.039
I'm here to help you.

00:11:17.039 --> 00:11:19.039
I'm here to help you.

00:11:19.039 --> 00:11:21.039
I'm here to help you.

00:11:22.039 --> 00:11:24.039
But it has to be your choice.

00:11:31.039 --> 00:11:32.039
Come with me, Kal-El.

00:11:38.039 --> 00:11:39.039
I can't do this.

00:11:43.039 --> 00:11:45.039
Just know...

00:11:45.039 --> 00:11:47.039
when you're ready,

00:11:47.039 --> 00:11:48.039
I'll be waiting for you.

00:11:51.039 --> 00:12:08.459
Orange is a good color for you, Dad.

00:12:09.399 --> 00:12:12.659
Although it might get a little old after 25 to life.

00:12:14.339 --> 00:12:16.659
I didn't ask you here to trade insults.

00:12:21.039 --> 00:12:29.980
No matter how wide the chasm gets between us, son,

00:12:30.919 --> 00:12:34.699
I'm your father. I'll always be your father.

00:12:34.919 --> 00:12:37.419
I'm the devil that's haunted me since the day I was born.

00:12:39.559 --> 00:12:41.279
Lex, this is not easy for me.

00:12:41.279 --> 00:12:41.379
I...

00:12:41.379 --> 00:12:49.279
As a father, I, um...

00:12:49.279 --> 00:12:53.299
I have failed you.

00:12:54.919 --> 00:12:56.539
I realize that now.

00:12:57.439 --> 00:12:58.959
And, uh...

00:12:58.959 --> 00:13:00.339
I'm sorry.

00:13:04.439 --> 00:13:08.600
Two years ago, I was diagnosed with a, um...

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:11.819
a degenerative liver disease.

00:13:13.879 --> 00:13:16.639
I've tried everything. Everything imaginable.

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:18.600
But, um...

00:13:19.279 --> 00:13:21.360
There's nothing.

00:13:23.059 --> 00:13:24.139
It's too late.

00:13:25.519 --> 00:13:27.879
No amount of money can save me.

00:13:35.439 --> 00:13:36.039
Lex.

00:13:37.159 --> 00:13:37.220
Please.

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.779
Don't let me die in prison.

00:13:48.419 --> 00:13:48.899
Don't.

00:13:48.899 --> 00:13:48.959
Don't.

00:13:48.959 --> 00:13:49.059
Don't.

00:13:49.059 --> 00:13:49.259
Don't.

00:13:49.259 --> 00:14:03.200
Dad

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:08.500
This might have been more effective

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:11.879
If you had a string quartet in the corner

00:14:11.879 --> 00:14:13.460
Playing Barber's Requiem

00:14:19.259 --> 00:14:21.559
I understand

00:14:21.559 --> 00:14:24.539
How could you trust me?

00:14:24.539 --> 00:14:27.179
I've asked my doctors to

00:14:27.179 --> 00:14:28.939
Release my medical files to you

00:14:28.939 --> 00:14:29.939
You can see for yourself

00:14:49.259 --> 00:15:01.460
She hasn't eaten anything since she's been here

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.379
Martha, right now her appetite is the least of our problems

00:15:04.379 --> 00:15:05.500
I think she's for real

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:07.919
I think Jor-El sent her

00:15:07.919 --> 00:15:08.860
Are you sure?

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.519
How else can we explain her powers?

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:11.919
Clark, this is Smallville

00:15:11.919 --> 00:15:14.039
Kryptonite's given a lot of people special abilities

00:15:14.039 --> 00:15:15.379
She knows my birth name

00:15:15.379 --> 00:15:16.580
She knows everything about me

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:18.939
She doesn't know anything more about you than Dr. Swan

00:15:18.939 --> 00:15:19.240
Dr. Swan?

00:15:20.139 --> 00:15:21.639
Do you think Swan sent Kara?

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.240
I have no idea what that man's agenda is

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:24.720
But wherever this girl is from

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:26.120
I just don't trust her

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.340
You're the one who cannot be trusted, Jonathan Kent

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:30.819
You broke the covenant

00:15:30.819 --> 00:15:33.600
Jor-El gave you many warnings

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.259
But you chose not to listen to them

00:15:35.259 --> 00:15:37.100
What is she talking about, Jonathan?

00:15:39.639 --> 00:15:41.019
Tell Kal-El what you did

00:15:41.019 --> 00:15:44.360
What kind of deal did you make, Dad?

00:15:49.259 --> 00:15:54.720
I promised Jor-El that if he gave me the power to bring you back from Metropolis

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:59.419
That one day I would return you to him

00:15:59.419 --> 00:16:01.700
Jonathan, you didn't do that

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:03.759
Martha, I had no idea it was going to be this soon

00:16:03.759 --> 00:16:04.139
No

00:16:04.139 --> 00:16:05.799
I told you, Kal-El

00:16:05.799 --> 00:16:07.720
They'll always betray you

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:10.419
Even the man you call your father

00:16:10.419 --> 00:16:12.399
I did not betray my son

00:16:12.399 --> 00:16:12.700
Quiet

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:16.879
Someone's listening

00:16:16.879 --> 00:16:19.139
What are you talking about?

00:16:19.259 --> 00:16:23.559
How'd you do that?

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.039
Who are you?

00:16:41.419 --> 00:16:42.679
Get out of my way!

00:16:49.259 --> 00:16:58.980
What did you do to him?

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:01.620
That man feared you, Kal-El

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.079
He wanted to exploit you

00:17:04.079 --> 00:17:05.079
So you killed him?

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:08.559
He didn't feel any pain

00:17:08.559 --> 00:17:17.119
She killed a man, Jonathan

00:17:17.119 --> 00:17:18.519
We have to call the sheriff

00:17:18.519 --> 00:17:19.000
What are we going to do?

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:19.099
What are we going to do?

00:17:19.099 --> 00:17:19.240
What are we going to do?

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:19.859
We're going to tell the sheriff

00:17:19.859 --> 00:17:22.980
Sweetheart, that a Kryptonian girl vaporized a federal agent

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.640
What have you invited into our lives?

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:29.559
Martha, I honestly don't believe I had another choice

00:17:29.559 --> 00:17:32.940
How could you have made a decision like that about our son without talking to me?

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:35.200
It was the only way that I could get him back

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:39.259
Why would you keep it a secret?

00:17:41.799 --> 00:17:44.839
Because I didn't want you to have to wait for the rest of your life

00:17:44.839 --> 00:17:47.500
Worrying about something that might not ever come to pass

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.980
Do you really think, Jonathan?

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.799
Do you really think Jor-El will ever give up on Clark?

00:17:50.839 --> 00:17:53.339
I can't just sit idly by while he tries to take away our son

00:17:53.339 --> 00:17:54.960
Well, we might not have a choice

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.559
That girl is more powerful than Clark

00:17:57.559 --> 00:18:11.180
Mr. Kent

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:13.599
So this is the legendary torch

00:18:13.599 --> 00:18:14.620
Yeah

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:17.319
A little less glamorous than you imagined, huh?

00:18:18.019 --> 00:18:18.819
If you're looking for a new one, you're going to have to go to the store

00:18:18.819 --> 00:18:19.339
I'm looking for Clark

00:18:19.339 --> 00:18:21.000
I haven't seen a trace of him

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:24.019
I was looking for you

00:18:24.019 --> 00:18:28.299
Something's telling me you're not here to throw a tea party

00:18:28.299 --> 00:18:31.559
Look, I understand that you're very good at getting to the bottom of things

00:18:31.559 --> 00:18:37.039
Do you think you could run the fingerprints off of this for me?

00:18:38.179 --> 00:18:38.960
No problem

